                    <chunk name="param_input" index="9">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Access" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">1</item>
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Optional roughness length z0 (m) PER WIND DIRECTION, aligned with Wind Directions. The terrain the wind crosses differs by sector — sea to the west, city to the east — and one z0 for all of them puts the wrong profile on most inlets. A single value applies to every direction; a shorter list repeats its last value. Leave empty to use Roughness Length / Terrain Type for all directions. Each direction case writes its own z0 into 0/ABLConditions (inlet profile AND ground wall function).</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">8ed1bc9f-f5b1-41de-bfc0-1919b96058e2</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">z0 per Direction</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">z0 [m]</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="1">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
                            <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                              <X>217</X>
                              <Y>634</Y>
                              <W>115</W>
                              <H>20</H>
                            </item>
                            <item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                              <X>276</X>
                              <Y>644</Y>
                            </item>
                          </items>
                        </chunk>
                      </chunks>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_input" index="10">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">The shape of the inflow. Log law (Richards &amp; Hoxey): OpenFOAM's atmBoundaryLayer inlet, k constant with height — the default and what every earlier study used. Harris &amp; Deaves (ESDU 01008): the strong-wind boundary layer of the UK National Annex to EN 1991-1-4, which the City of London Wind Microclimate Guidelines (2019) require — a gradient-height term on the mean speed and the measured strong-wind turbulence, written as fixedProfile tables for U, k (3/2·σu², so the gust Eddy3D reads from k is the Harris &amp; Deaves gust) and epsilon. Each direction gets its own table from its own speed and z0, and the cases sample the profile approaching the model so the Study Report can plot simulated against target, as the guideline asks.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">a0b88afa-f711-4115-b3fd-b9c89589d1dc</item>
                        <item name="Multiple" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Inlet Profile</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Profile</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="Options" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Log law (Richards &amp; Hoxey)
Harris &amp; Deaves (ESDU 01008)</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                        <item name="Value" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Log law (Richards &amp; Hoxey)</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="2">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
