                    <chunk name="param_input" index="9">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Perturb the inflow face with zero-mean synthetic turbulence at the log law's own intensity (I_u = 1/ln((z+z0)/z0), 18 % at z = z0 x 240), so the LES is fed fluctuations instead of a steady profile. On AIJ Case A this took the wake's bias from +0.64 to +0.07 and the reattachment length from 1.3 H to 0.6 H (tunnel 0.4-0.75 H); costs ~45 % more time on a discrete GPU. Off = the steady log law (the validation control).</item>
