                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Purpose: Wind around buildings on the GPU, watched live in the viewport.
Fidelity: Engineering - transient lattice-Boltzmann CFD, not validated for this site; FluidX3D's licence excludes commercial use.
Method: LBM Case with FluidX3D Run Settings: 2 m grid, 720 s simulated, ABL inflow of 5 m/s at 10 m.
Result: FluidX3D Live View colours a probe mesh while it runs; Scalar and Vector Field Viewers show probed values.
Needs: Eddy3D Setup &gt; LBM CFD (FluidX3D), built locally; needs a GPU. Runtime: minutes.
Edit: Geometry, grid spacing, simulated time, inflow.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
